.TH ADMIT 1
.SH NAME
admit \- place a work in the library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B admit
.I FILE
.RB [ \-b
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-i ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Signs
.I FILE
with
.I ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
and places it in
.IR /library/outer .
Prints the work ID.
.PP
.I FILE
must lie in the cell. It stays there after admission.
.PP
A file named
.IB NAME .json
that is a well-formed rite is admitted as a rite. A file named
.IB NAME .table
of 64 lines, each 1 to 64 printable characters, is admitted as a table; see yarrow(1).
Any other file is admitted as text.
.PP
Bytes admitted count against the allowance. One admission per life.
.PP
Requires grade adept.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " ID"
Burn work
.I ID
to make room. Required when the library is full.
.TP
.BI \-s " FILE"
Seal
.I FILE
with the work.
.TP
.B \-i
Place the work in
.I /library/inner
instead.
.SH FILES
/library/catalog, /chapter/burnlog
.SH SEE ALSO
burn(1), prove(1), yarrow(1), metacog(1)
